module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set

import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "**a witness module that discriminates correctly is absent from the runner's executed set** (THE CHECK IS RIGHT, ITS ARMS ARE ENROLLED, AND ITS SUBJECT IS REAL -- the only missing thing is membership in the population the required run actually schedules, so every signal a reader consults says covered and none of them is what decides.",

    "THE INVALID STATE is a claim module present on disk, correct, and named in no schedule the required lane reads. The harm is that a green verdict is cited as coverage for the class that module owns. A floor verdict names what it EXECUTED; it cannot name what it never saw, and the reader supplies the missing quantifier without noticing.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 2 on paper and BELOW THE LADDER in fact. The mechanism exists and would fire; DESIGN.md section 4b(2) makes rung 2 conditional on that mechanism EXECUTING and STAYING ENROLLED, so an unenrolled wall holds no rung at all. This is the inert-lens tier the design document names: the machinery exists and nothing gates on it.",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#10688. Hand-authored consumers still read `item_registry` by bare leaf after the registry was re-keyed on declaration identity, so the whole-graph read missed every time and every row silently took the unexpanded local entry. `test.claim.resolved_rust_fn_service_chain_consumer_witness` CATCHES THIS -- rebuilding with the fix reverted turns its shallow arm red -- and it was green across the whole branch, because the module appears nowhere in `src/v2/workflow/` and therefore never enters the executed set. `verdict=FloorClean` over the claim corpus was silent about it, and a cross-module claim added in the same PR inherited the dormancy: the planned figure stayed unchanged across the PR that added the claim.",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING FACT, and the reason this is its own row rather than an instance of a narrow-subject check: THE WITNESS AND THE CLASS ARE PRESENT AND CORRECT. Nothing about the check is wrong. A reader who opens the file finds discriminating arms, a red control and an accurate name; a reader who greps the corpus finds the class covered; a reader who reads the floor verdict finds it clean. The defect is a JOIN that nobody performs -- claim modules on disk against claim modules scheduled -- and it is invisible from either side alone. Compare [[discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled]], where the file itself withholds the arm, and [[a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism]].",

    "THE CHEAP DETECTOR is a set difference the runner could compute for free: claim modules discovered on disk MINUS claim modules the required lanes schedule, printed with the verdict. Any non-empty remainder is a population the green does not speak for. The floor already prints `outside_this_runs_universe`, so the shape exists; what is missing is that a module absent from every schedule never reaches that accounting at all -- it is outside the universe of the thing that reports being outside the universe.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: before citing a green run as coverage for a class, ask which SCHEDULE named the claim, not which file declares it. A claim's existence and a claim's execution are separate facts, and only the latter is what a verdict reports.",

    "FURTHER INDEPENDENT INSTANCES OF THE SAME SHAPE IN THE SAME NIGHT, which is the argument that this is a class and not a coincidence: a check whose FORM is right and whose POPULATION is narrower than its name implies. The others, found by other lanes, each named: regen asking the filesystem a question `seed_retention_frontier` owns; doc_reachability asserting duplicate-key rather than slug-to-file; heal reporting SUCCESS on a head where build was red, because heal does not install that population. Each was individually reasonable and none was written down as a population claim, which is exactly why they could all stand at once.)",

    "THE SAME ABSENCE HIDES REDS, NOT ONLY FALSE GREENS, and that is another harm this row did not state. Every instance above is a CORRECT check whose green is cited as coverage; the absence is dangerous because nobody learns the class is unchecked. But a module outside the executed set is also free to BREAK and stay broken: nothing reports it, so the file rots in place while reading as ordinary committed evidence. gunbc#11025, 2026-09-11: witnesses in `v2.test.claim.long.accumulator_copy_compile_gate` failed at evaluation with `no field 'kind' on type 'NormalizedTree'` -- a real defect, loud when run -- and had been failing for an unknown length of time. The entry is a `LegacyFrozenPathDeferral` in `gunbc.witness.witness_deferral_freeze`, admitted by PATH POLICY with no executing consumer, so every witness in that module executes nowhere in any required lane and the failures could sit red indefinitely. The repair was a field-level change; the reason it survived was membership.",

    "SO THE ADMISSION MECHANISM MATTERS, AND IT IS NOT ALWAYS AN OMISSION. The instances above are modules nobody scheduled -- a gap. This instance was scheduled OUT, deliberately, by a path-policy rule that admits an entry as deferred: the roster that records it is itself the evidence, and it is honest about what it is. The class is the same because the consequence is identical (no executing consumer), but the DETECTION differs: a gap is found by joining modules-on-disk to modules-scheduled, while a deferral is already written down and needs only to be read as what it says. A deferral roster is therefore a list of modules whose reds nobody will see, and it can be consulted directly rather than derived.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-10-07, the same absence HIDING A STANDING RED, and the strongest form of that later harm. test.claim.self_host_emitted_call_target_realization_witness::w_depth_one_shared_field_refutation_stays_shape_guarded FAILS against main at the IMMUTABLE sha 1728bcc0ab4e7d8285359f161612d4c1226812f2 (Gate parse_acceptance_census: accepted arm on a minimal module, #13415) -- claim_batch claim-run at that sha went red, BuildBuddy remote dispatch completed 2026-10-07T08:27:47.537Z, discovering session vivid-lynx-377 job j36fc601a, command and output retained in the session transcript -- and every unrepaired descendant of that sha inherits the red. No STANDING gate executed it: the ordinary prepared subject excludes modules outside the required-gate closure, and changed-witness selection replaces that disposition only when a diff selects the identity -- which is exactly how the red surfaced: an unrelated PR touched the entry's sibling probes, inherited defunct-import reds from the #13388 re-homing, and ran the whole set. The failing witness synthesizes a std-types-only probe (a shared coproduct matched at shallow depth inside a record pattern) and imports neither v2.std.optional nor any renamed spelling; the red predates every edit on the discovering branch. THE HONEST CEILING IS RUNG 2: a red witness on main stays writable -- a scheduled full-corpus lane would only expose and block it -- so rung 3 is not on offer. THE HONEST NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER is that lane IMPLEMENTED AND ENROLLED, not a sign-off: a standing claim run over a DEFINED CLAIM-ROOT POPULATION that refuses, or invokes a declared remedy, on every red or non-verdict, DEMONSTRATED FAILING on a planted or standing red. Manual attribution -- running the entry on main's own tree before blaming the discovering PR -- is how this specimen was found, and it is a discipline, not a rung.",

    "POPULATION FORM OF THE SAME JOIN FAILURE, and the specimen that generalises it. Found 2026-10-19 by the CHEAP DETECTOR above, run at origin/main 45fdd50224891a6414e00ddd01132493e1113233: a set of modules that declare test fn bodies, sit inside a witness_layer_roots layer (dag, src/v2), are named by no execution roster, and fall outside every witness_discovery_scan_dirs entry. Every body in that population is a real discriminating assertion that CI never executes. The population, by module: src/v2/workflow/orchestration_retry_emit.dag, src/v2/workflow/orchestration_emit.dag, src/v2/workflow/orchestration_bash.dag, src/v2/workflow/orchestration_tier2_emit.dag, src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag (since deleted by commit e669356d5d0, landing with pull request #14688; re-derive at a head after it for the remainder), src/v2/lens/mandatory_tag/corpus_scan_witness.dag, src/v2/lens/realization_vocabulary_containment.dag. The counts of modules and bodies are NOT transcribed here (DESIGN.md section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output): re-derive them by running the CHEAP DETECTOR -- the set difference over the Node tree against gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots's witness_discovery_scan_dirs and witness_layer_roots -- at any head, and cite the run, not this row. What the row asserts is the CLASS: each such module compiles cleanly while no test fn reaches the runner, so every signal a reader consults -- the file compiles, it has tests, the floor is clean -- says covered, and the only signal that decides (presence in the executed set) is the signal nobody reads.",

    "HOW THIS SPECIMEN WAS FOUND, which is the point. It was not looked for: it surfaced while reading src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag at 0dc3f0ab4c1fe112c13b10d6cbc991a94f3744fd to decide whether a deletion was safe, and deleting the production route through that file's sole bracket operator turned NOTHING red anywhere -- compiles stayed clean and no witness moved from red to green or back. Ceiling, stated so the row does not talk itself out of the check it asks for: the condition is mechanically preventable, so an enrolled coherence witness over it sits at RUNG 2, not rung 3 -- a module in a witness_layer_roots layer that declares test fn bodies, lies outside every witness_discovery_scan_dirs entry and is named by no execution roster is decidable from the Node tree plus gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots. It is absent because it changes what CI executes and pays for, which is an operator call wider than a ledger row -- not because the fact is unreadable. gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots already distinguishes deliberately-non-executing namespaces (non_executing_witness_module_prefixes = \"v1\"), so 'unrun on purpose' versus 'unrun by accident' is expressible in the authority and simply unenforced for the layer roots.",

    "COUNTING DISCIPLINE THIS ROW OWES, because the naive figure is wrong and was nearly used. The detector has a path filter and a scan-dir filter, and only the latter decides: dropping the path filter (*/test/*, a PATH filter, NOT the scan-dir filter) silently widens the population to every ordinary claim module under dag/ and src/v2/, which is not the class; the intended population survives precisely because the scan-dir filter is applied, since every scan dir sits under a test path. Part of the population overlaps dag/gunbc/witness/witness_row_cost_basis.tsv, itself a dated reading at a named commit. No counts from the detector are transcribed in this row (DESIGN.md section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output) -- any figure a reader wants is re-derived by running the named instrument at the head in question, and the heads named in this row (origin/main 45fdd5022489 for the population, 0dc3f0ab4c1f for the discovery) are pins for re-derivation, never copied forward as authority.",

    "WHAT THE PORTED COVERAGE IS AND IS NOT, stated so nobody reads it as production safety: the test module of pull request #14489, test.claim.path_predicate_bash_lowering_witness (its dirname-ascent tests pin the lowered bytes exactly and include the POSIX-name guards) -- landed as d0581390cd0 on 2026-10-23, so it is executing coverage on main, and what those tests are is stated below -- exercise a TYPED SUBSTRATE WITH NO PRODUCTION CALLER. Nothing emitted today passes through bash_path_predicate_target_model or bash_dirname_ascent_target_model: the production line that used them was deleted as a no-consumer chain, and the only remaining callers were src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag, which CI never discovered, and that witness itself. They are coverage of a substrate kept for a hypothetical future typed path-test route, plus a guard against a future emitter shipping d;rm -rf / into an emitted program if that route is ever taken -- NOT evidence that any emitted program is safe today, and they must not be cited as if they were.",

    "ISLAND NAMED AS THE DELETION TRIGGER'S POPULATION -- PROPOSED, NOT BUILT, AND HEADED AS MEASURED. SPECIMEN, AND THE FORWARD REFERENCE IS LABELLED AS PENDING. DATED HISTORICAL READING, main at the pinned head 0dc3f0ab4c1f (2026-10-19): src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag was present there and PROPOSED for deletion as a module guarding no production route -- on the stacked carve branch session/zesty-tern-692-pr7, which carries pull request #14688, it was already absent. The while_emit body reading taken at 0dc3f0ab4c1f was a live fact about the module at that dated head, produced by the CHEAP DETECTOR named above and deliberately not transcribed here. DELETION RECEIPT, beside that reading and dated: the proposal was executed on the carve by commit e669356d5d0 (2026-10-20), which deleted src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag and lands with pull request #14688; re-running the CHEAP DETECTOR at any head that contains that commit returns the remainder of the population. The while_emit body reading stays as the dated measurement of the pinned head 0dc3f0ab4c1f it always claimed to be, and the arm it tested (PipelineStep::While plus orch_emit_while_step in v2.compiler.emit_orchestration) survives deliberately as the declared frontier of gunbc.plans.for_while_loop_sugar. Scope, in the order the consumers fall away: once while_emit is gone, the dirname/cmdsubst-call chain (bash_dirname_ascent_target_model, orch_cmdsubst_assign_call_target_model, orch_call_target_model) and the PathPredicate ladder that only while_emit entered had only test callers, so they formed a dangling unit -- what actually happened instead is that the byte assertions were re-pinned against the surviving lowering functions in test.claim.path_predicate_bash_lowering_witness (#14489) before the module went; deleting dead code together with the tests that only test it is NOT the defect this row files, because nothing survives untested. TRIGGER -- what dissolves this row: an operator CI-policy decision. Either (a) add src/v2/workflow (and the src/v2/lens files) to witness_discovery_scan_dirs, which makes the assertions execute but pulls in the whole self-witnessed family and its cost; (b) delete the population along with the code it guards; or (c) install the rung-2 coherence witness above so an unrun self-witness refuses at compile time. The decision is outward-facing (it changes what CI executes and pays for) and belongs to the operator, not to whoever notices. Until then the population has no entry point at all, and the missing .dag producer plus its gunbc test label is the follow-up that turns it into an instrument. The kept While arm earns its own falsifier when for_while_loop_sugar gives it a real constructor; until then it is a plan frontier, not coverage.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-10-23, THE CLASS HAS NOT HEALED: the set-difference detector this row proposed (claim modules on disk MINUS claim modules scheduled) is still not running, and another standing red sat on main a day. THE MODULE: v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_application_argument_inhabitance_witness, a claim module over the application-argument inhabitance doors -- the class this seat (Seat 16, N7 infer wall) owns. THE JOIN, performed by hand as the row's recognition rule demands: the module matches no family prefix (every family row in src/v2/workflow/required_floor.dag is a `test.claim.` v1 path; the file's own admission comment records the same shape for v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0), and it appears in no required_gate_authored_modules row -- measured, not inferred: no module under src/v2/test/claim/compiler/ is named in required_floor.dag. THE REDS: claims fail against main -- infer_generic_formal_instantiation_refuses_a_non_inhabiting_argument_holds and infer_type_variable_inside_an_arrow_formal_is_counted_frontier_holds broke at c5d5b2025e4e #14749 (2026-10-22; PASSing at its parent 05e1339b88ae), and infer_bare_int_at_an_optional_formal_refuses_holds broke at 388263b185c #14644 (the Optional stack, Rule A part 3): MEASURED by the manager's execution bisect -- PASSES at its parent b96b5b6a4068, FAILS at 388263b185c, which settles an earlier round that had only narrowed the break to a commit window ee5456eea3a8 #14662 .. fc808362fc53 (the endpoints of #14662 PASSed there, excluding #14662 and #14756). THE VERDICT ON (b) IS FIXTURE DRIFT, NOT REGRESSION -- GROUNDED ON LANDED PRODUCERS, NOT ON THE SCRATCH PROBE THAT SUGGESTED IT: v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_application_argument_inhabitance_witness claim infer_bare_int_at_an_optional_formal_refuses_holds, once its asserted reason follows #14644's typed reason (^infer_literal_at_optional_is_not_present, minted in v2.compiler.infer's InferLiteralElaborationRefused cause), is REPRODUCIBLE by claim_batch on that module -- the claim itself is the instrument; and the same reason is pinned independently by GREEN source-route claims in v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_arm_close_witness (rb_x1, rb_x3, rc8), which run on landed code. The tree still REFUSES -- no silent widen; a bare Int at Int? refuses exactly as explicit_present_is_the_authoring_policy demands. (The scratch fatal-namer localized the reason before any other route, but is never-merge scratch and is not cited as the grounding.) An earlier version of this receipt named #14662 as prime suspect on file-edit proximity; the bisect refuted that too, and the correction is kept visible here because proximate-edit suspicion is exactly the reasoning an unexecuted claim module invites. No lane saw any of it; FloorClean never spoke about the module. THE MERGE CAUSATION THIS INSTANCE ADDS: #14749 itself is what broke some of the claims -- a change to v2.compiler.infer whose own evidence base included claims that contradict its new rules. Had the module had an executing consumer, its red would have BLOCKED #14749 at merge, not sat on main for a day until it was noticed by accident. THE DISCOVERY CHANNEL is the row's recognition rule working by hand: a different lane (Seat 16) was mirroring the module's accepted fixture in a scratch probe to discriminate a DIFFERENT defect (the generic-formal shape arm's mint), the mirror refused where the original was supposed to refuse, and the manager's manual claim_batch run over the original module -- attribution, the discipline, not the rung -- went red on named claims while the rest PASSed. THE REPAIR IS SEQUENCED, NOT SKIPPED: the boundary verdict on the failing claims comes ahead of the bisection: (most assert pre-#14749 behavior that the RFM generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2 -- the row #14749 closes -- documents as the DEFECT SYMPTOM, so -- per §4d, marked as inference not yet deduced -- they are EXPECTED fixture drift pending their claim_batch re-runs on fixed assertions, exactly as (b) was settled; the remainder is bisected to 388263b185c #14644 (the Optional stack) by execution, then rewrite or retire them, THEN admit the module at exact module grain in required_gate_authored_modules() with the pricing comment (claim eval steps, preparation wall, measured on srv1 at enrolment). The admission is green-lit in principle by the manager and deliberately withheld until the module is green on main, because a gate that fails on the day it lands is not a gate. THIS INSTANCE IS THE ROW'S OWN ARGUMENT REPEATED: the cheap detector was written down in 2026-09 and the next standing red of this class arrived 2026-10-22 with nothing between them.",

  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_discovery_scan_dirs"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_layer_roots"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "non_executing_witness_module_prefixes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.emit_orchestration", decl_name: "orch_emit_while_step"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.orchestration_retry_emit", decl_name: "orch_retry_byte_identical_to_hand_authored_holds"),
  ],
}
